---
import Layout from "~/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Footer from "~/components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "~/components/Header.astro";
import Hero from "~/components/Hero.astro";
import ScrollReveal from "~/components/ScrollReveal.astro";

const BASE_URL = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout
  title="Mentor AI"
  description="Research-backed AI-mediated feedback for open-ended writing: FeedbackWriter for instructors and TAs, DraftMentors for students, with human judgment and rubrics in the loop."
>
  <Header />
  <main
    id="main-content"
    role="main"
    class="bg-background flex-1 pt-12 pb-24 md:pt-20 md:pb-40"
  >
    <Hero />
    <section
      class="mx-auto max-w-none border-t border-gray-200/80 p-16 lg:max-w-6xl"
      aria-labelledby="problem-heading"
    >
      <ScrollReveal>
        <h2
          id="problem-heading"
          class="text-umich-blue text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl"
        >
          Why feedback is hard to scale
        </h2>
      </ScrollReveal>
      <div class="mt-8 max-w-3xl text-pretty text-gray-700">
        <ScrollReveal delay={0.06}>
          <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed">
            Formative feedback supports learning in <strong
              class="font-medium text-gray-900">open-ended writing</strong
            >, but producing it well takes sustained attention from instructors
            and teaching assistants, especially in large courses.
          </p>
        </ScrollReveal>
        <ScrollReveal delay={0.1}>
          <p class="mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed">
            Automated comments can be fast but risky: they can misread
            discipline-specific reasoning or drift from your rubric, and they
            may not provide the kind of guidance students can use to revise.
            What we need is not automation alone, but <strong
              class="font-medium text-gray-900">human judgment</strong
            > steering <strong class="font-medium text-gray-900"
              >AI assistance</strong
            >.
          </p>
        </ScrollReveal>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section
      class="mx-auto max-w-none border-t border-gray-200/80 bg-white/50 p-16 lg:max-w-6xl"
      aria-labelledby="solution-teaser-heading"
    >
      <ScrollReveal>
        <h2
          id="solution-teaser-heading"
          class="text-umich-blue text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl"
        >
          Our approach
        </h2>
      </ScrollReveal>
      <ScrollReveal delay={0.06}>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg text-pretty text-gray-700">
          We build tools where AI drafts suggestions under your rubrics, and
          teaching staff review, correct, and align those suggestions before
          they become student-facing feedback. Students can also get structured
          support through DraftMentors, consistent with how you define the task.
        </p>
      </ScrollReveal>
      <ScrollReveal delay={0.1}>
        <ul
          class="mt-8 max-w-3xl list-disc space-y-3 pl-6 text-pretty text-gray-700"
        >
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-900">Instructors</strong> define assignments
            and rubrics.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-900">TAs / graders</strong> use FeedbackWriter
            to shape rubric-faithful feedback from AI suggestions.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-900">Students</strong> revise with guidance,
            including DraftMentors where available.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </ScrollReveal>
      <ScrollReveal delay={0.14}>
        <a
          href={`${BASE_URL}solution/`}
          class="text-umich-blue mt-8 inline-block text-sm font-semibold hover:underline"
        >
          Explore the full workflow →
        </a>
      </ScrollReveal>
    </section>
    <section
      class="mx-auto max-w-none p-16 lg:max-w-6xl"
      aria-labelledby="research-teaser-heading"
    >
      <ScrollReveal>
        <h2
          id="research-teaser-heading"
          class="text-umich-blue text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl"
        >
          Evidence from a real course
        </h2>
      </ScrollReveal>
      <ScrollReveal delay={0.06}>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg text-pretty text-gray-700">
          In a randomized controlled trial in a large introductory economics
          course (<strong class="font-medium text-gray-900">N = 354</strong>),
          students who received AI-mediated feedback through FeedbackWriter
          produced <strong class="font-medium text-gray-900"
            >significantly higher-quality revisions</strong
          > than those who received human-only TA feedback (Cohen’s d = 0.50 in the
          paper (about the 50th to 70th percentile shift as reported there). Course
          post-test scores <strong class="font-medium text-gray-900"
            >did not differ significantly</strong
          > between conditions; see the publication for full results and methods.
        </p>
      </ScrollReveal>
      <ScrollReveal delay={0.1}>
        <a
          href={`${BASE_URL}research/`}
          class="text-umich-blue mt-6 inline-block text-sm font-semibold hover:underline"
        >
          Publications and findings →
        </a>
      </ScrollReveal>
    </section>
    <section
      class="mx-auto max-w-none border-t border-gray-200/80 bg-white/50 p-16 lg:max-w-6xl"
      aria-labelledby="impact-heading"
    >
      <ScrollReveal>
        <h2
          id="impact-heading"
          class="text-umich-blue text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl"
        >
          What this can mean for your course
        </h2>
      </ScrollReveal>
      <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2" role="list">
        <li class="flex items-stretch">
          <ScrollReveal delay={0.05}>
            <p
              class="h-full rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 text-pretty text-gray-700 shadow-sm"
            >
              <strong class="text-umich-blue block text-base font-semibold"
                >Rubric alignment</strong
              >
              <span class="mt-2 block">
                Suggestions are grounded in criteria you set, not a generic
                writing coach.
              </span>
            </p>
          </ScrollReveal>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-stretch">
          <ScrollReveal delay={0.1}>
            <p
              class="h-full rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 text-pretty text-gray-700 shadow-sm"
            >
              <strong class="text-umich-blue block text-base font-semibold"
                >TA capacity</strong
              >
              <span class="mt-2 block">
                AI assistance can reduce repetitive drafting work, helping
                graders focus on rubric-aligned judgment and correction.
              </span>
            </p>
          </ScrollReveal>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-stretch">
          <ScrollReveal delay={0.15}>
            <p
              class="h-full rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 text-pretty text-gray-700 shadow-sm"
            >
              <strong class="text-umich-blue block text-base font-semibold"
                >Revision quality</strong
              >
              <span class="mt-2 block">
                In our RCT, revised drafts improved more under AI-mediated
                feedback than under human-only feedback (as measured in the
                study).
              </span>
            </p>
          </ScrollReveal>
        </li>
        <li class="flex items-stretch">
          <ScrollReveal delay={0.2}>
            <p
              class="h-full rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white p-6 text-pretty text-gray-700 shadow-sm"
            >
              <strong class="text-umich-blue block text-base font-semibold"
                >Research grounding</strong
              >
              <span class="mt-2 block">
                Claims on this site follow published methods and results. We do
                not add metrics that are not in the papers.
              </span>
            </p>
          </ScrollReveal>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section
      class="mx-auto max-w-none p-16 lg:max-w-6xl"
      aria-labelledby="home-cta-heading"
    >
      <ScrollReveal>
        <div
          class="border-umich-blue/25 bg-umich-blue rounded-lg px-6 py-12 text-center text-white shadow-md md:px-12"
        >
          <h2 id="home-cta-heading" class="text-2xl font-semibold sm:text-3xl">
            Join us in improving feedback in education
          </h2>
          <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-pretty text-white/90">
            Instructors, departments, and collaborators: tell us about your
            course or research interests. We read every message we can respond
            to.
          </p>
          <a
            href={`${BASE_URL}signup/`}
            class="bg-umich-maize text-umich-blue focus-visible:ring-umich-maize mt-8 inline-block rounded-md px-8 py-3 text-sm font-semibold transition hover:bg-white focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2"
          >
            Join us
          </a>
        </div>
      </ScrollReveal>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
